==National elevation ranges==
Of all countries, [[Lesotho]] has the world's highest low point at {{convert|1,400.|m}}. Other countries with high low points include [[Rwanda]] {{convert|950.|m}} and [[Andorra]] {{convert|840.|m}}. Countries with very low high points include [[Maldives]] {{convert|5.|m}}, [[Tuvalu]], {{convert|5.|m}} and the [[Marshall Islands]] {{convert|10.|m}}. These island countries also have the smallest range between their lowest (sea level) and highest points, and are very sensitive to changes in sea level.

The highest and lowest points in [[China]] constitute the greatest elevation range within any single country at {{convert|9002.|m}}. The elevation ranges are also great in [[Nepal]] {{convert|8789.|m}}, [[Pakistan]] {{convert|8611.|m}}, and [[India]] {{convert|8588.7|m}}.

[[Monaco]]'s elevation range is among the greatest relative to surface area. Within its 2.02&nbsp;km<sup>2</sup> territory, there is a difference of 140&nbsp;m between its highest and lowest points.

